# Customer-local artifacts: NEVER commit. The gap-scout subagent + learned-
# rules system writes here, and these MUST stay out of the skill repo so
# `git pull` doesn't clobber customer-discovered rules.
#
# Canonical location is ~/.tableau-to-sigma/ (user home dir), but if someone
# accidentally sets TABLEAU_TO_SIGMA_HOME to a path inside this repo or runs
# the scripts from here, the artifacts would land here. This .gitignore
# catches that.
.tableau-to-sigma/
learned-rules.yaml
escalations/

# Test artifacts from validate-sigma-formula.rb / scout-validate-and-persist.rb
scout-test-home/
scout-tests/
*-scout-test.json
*-scout-spec.json

# Local conversion artifacts (intermediate state from a real customer run)
# typically lives in /tmp/<workbook>/ but if someone runs from inside this
# directory:
*-gaps-report.md
*-gaps.json
*-actions.md
specs-*.json
wb-spec.json
wb-spec-*.json
chart-specs-*.json
dashboard-layout-*.json
dashboard-layout-*-meta.json
*.log
runs/

# Field-run litter at the skill root: run workdirs (connection/intake/doctor
# state carries customer identifiers) and extract-read litter. workdir-*/ is
# backstopped by tools/lint-tree-litter.sh, which fails if one is ever
# *tracked*; *.hyper has NO tracked-file backstop yet (the lint's regex has no
# .hyper arm) — this ignore rule is the only guard, so never `git add -f` an
# extract.
workdir-*/
*.hyper
# …but corpus-committed .hyper fixtures stay trackable.
!corpus/**/*.hyper

# Cross-run registries + any other skill-root run state — machine-local by
# design, never committed (see CONTRIBUTING.md "Run state stays local").
probe-artifacts.jsonl
posted-workbooks.jsonl
offramps.jsonl
phase-metrics.jsonl
/*.jsonl
